+# dc-kotlin-manifest-version
+
+Locks the cross-file version contract of one Kotlin generation: the
+Kotlin Gradle plugin version the generated `build.gradle.kts` declares
+(feature spec 24, ruling 8) and the `kotlin-stdlib` version the
+generated Maven POM declares (feature spec 25, `emitMaven`) must be the
+same version, because both files are written by the same compilation.
+
+## The two version sites (base `e1c65975`)
+
+| file (relative to the worktree) | line | bytes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `packages/compiler/reflaxe/kotlin/kotlincompiler/Compiler.hx` | 417 | `+ "    kotlin(\"jvm\") version \"2.4.10\"\n"` (the `build.gradle.kts` plugin line) |
+| `packages/compiler/PackageArtifacts.hx` | 388 | `lines.push("      <version>2.4.10</version>");` (the `kotlin-stdlib` dependency inside `pom()`) |
+
+Both are literal strings in the emitter; there is no shared constant,
+which is exactly why a single-sided edit (or a future single-sided
+upgrade) is possible and why the comparison must be mechanical.
+
+## Files
+
+- `check.sh` — the check. `check.sh <build.gradle.kts> <pom>` parses the
+  two versions **separately** (the Gradle plugin line; the
+  `org.jetbrains.kotlin:kotlin-stdlib` dependency block of the POM, with
+  the project-level `<version>` explicitly out of scope) and compares
+  them. Exit `0` equal, `1` mismatch (single-sided change), `2` usage or
+  parse error. It never reads the host toolchain.
+- `run.sh` — one isolated run: one generation into
+  `out/dc-kotlin-manifest-version/` (the example `kotlin.hxml` with the
+  output trees moved under `out/` plus `-D package-artifacts=emit -D
+  package-kotlinc=<abs> -D package-group=dev.boring`, the same shape
+  `tests/ts/package-artifacts.test.ts` drives), the positive control,
+  the POM-only mutated negative control (required by the task), and a
+  supplementary Gradle-only mutated negative control. Every stage saves
+  argv, cwd, separated stdout/stderr, the exit code, and input sha256;
+  the mutation stages save the mutated file's before/after hashes and
+  the diff. Each invocation creates a fresh evidence directory
+  `<evidence-root>/<utc-timestamp>-<pid>/`.
+
+## Usage
+
+From the worktree root, inside the nix develop shell:
+
+```sh
+bash tests/package/dc-kotlin-manifest-version/run.sh <evidence-root>
+```
+
+Exit `0` when the generation succeeds, the positive control passes, and
+both negative controls fail as required; `3` otherwise.
+
+## Host kotlinc is not a manifest version
+
+`package-kotlinc` (spec 25) names the host compiler that packs the jar;
+it floats with the build environment. Spec 24 ruling 9 states the
+Gradle plugin version is a *dialect floor* ("the oldest dialect the
+current toolchain verified"), not a claim about the host compiler.
+`run.sh` records `kotlinc -version` in `00-host-identity` precisely to
+keep the two concepts apart in the evidence, and `check.sh` never
+consults it.
